#{[17592186381001 #edb/ref 1080 "343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381001 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381001 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26a7dd9b-e017-5f3a-8ac2-116d68520887" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381002 #edb/ref 1080 "207" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381002 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381002 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6842fe58-1814-5da0-b2b5-e8aa3f1ea7d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381003 #edb/ref 1080 "125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381003 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381003 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "357c1cd9-e42d-5c09-8c34-8eb3c6795c39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381004 #edb/ref 1080 "144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381004 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381004 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "34c8f94b-393d-56a8-88a1-afd8c3474d44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381005 #edb/ref 1080 "243" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381005 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381005 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "64ec3eb1-c941-574f-b566-b7540e15ac84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186381014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132417" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1071 "${\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2y}^{y+1}2xy\\,dx\\,dy=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "86450b76-caa8-5dc8-9785-42134807827a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381013 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{2y}^{y+1}2xy\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}y[{\\int }_{2y}^{y+1}2x\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}y[\\,{x}^{2}\\,]_{2y}^{y+1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}y((y+1)^{2}-(2y)^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}y({y}^{2}+2y+1-4{y}^{2})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-3{y}^{3}+2{y}^{2}+y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}(-3{y}^{3}+2{y}^{2}+y)\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{3}{4}{y}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{-1}^{0} \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{11}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381014 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "36c24fc7-d1a1-5f71-a6ea-af647a4e2a84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381015 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381015 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381015 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5b623f36-eb68-544e-a7e5-05d9acdf0e7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381016 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{7}{12}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381016 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381016 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3b2f28b-4079-5eb5-984a-4af170512514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381017 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{11}{12}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381017 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381017 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9504c561-f825-5c73-ab9f-071939988f76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381018 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381018 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381018 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb5e9db7-bd7d-592b-a932-d8249d8253cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381019 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381019 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381019 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ce36cb26-a73b-51ff-8442-c8e214bc0969" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186381021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132497" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9f/9fb82d3ef2fa47cc67e04ae7c43bb2f0fe021adb73063107f9ad16e9627cc451.png)\n\nIf $D$ is the finite region enclosed between the curves $x=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1$ and $x={y}^{2}-2,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown above, then ${∬}_{D}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dA=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "808843b5-4ec6-51d5-9767-8d30c84390fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381020 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's represent $D$ as a type II region. \n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1 & ={y}^{2}-2 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}{y}^{2}-3 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)(y+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are\n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/9e/9ed5a24f07ad025cbf47d664ac2c9e2f6525e43b0bc73c0b25eb7e3e5c60ac47.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,{y}^{2}-2\\le x\\le \\frac{1}{4}{y}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381021 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "944e9043-a2b2-5890-9087-b38a43ff9304" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381022 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381022 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381022 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81410832-b6b3-5770-a5c8-ab39c78cd75a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381023 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/4+1}^{{y}^{2}-2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381023 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381023 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa8f5140-7e4d-5c07-9a35-b2c5c8c58b49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381024 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381024 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381024 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4a5c0904-845d-5506-b9ed-cbbf441c4201" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381025 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381025 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381025 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0abdda0e-9501-5f4b-a759-4d62540e6335" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381026 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-2}^{{y}^{2}/4+1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-{y}^{2})\\,dx]dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381026 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381026 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3eec9544-9a54-5558-87b3-c7be335e7ad3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186381028 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132516" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the finite region $D$ in the $xy$-plane enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt{-x}$ and the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3),$ above the $x$-axis. What is ${∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA\\,$ expressed as a repeated integral?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c102617-2635-5783-b418-6ddb6be7b181" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381027 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's make a sketch of our region.\n\n![](images/c4/c4531d05ef2634d04e590b099ba5ec0269c9c00f12dce82442043cad4377db1a.png)\n\nWe need to represent $D$ as a type II region. Writing $y=\\sqrt{-x}$ and $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3)$ in terms of $y,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=\\sqrt{-x} & \\,⟹\\,x=-{y}^{2} \\\\ y=\\frac{1}{2}(x+3) & \\,⟹\\,x=2y-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{y}^{2} & =2y-3 \\\\ {y}^{2}+2y-3 & =0 \\\\ (y+3)(y-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/31/3187c1520326caf6d009cacaf8b13bfc58a3e0eadbbdfd7aab01fb0d4154f476.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,2y-3\\le x\\le -{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381029 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186381033 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186381030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381028 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ec70df83-3cc5-54d5-84b9-e21b1cbe078e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381029 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381029 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381029 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e34dcd5c-c548-555f-9d01-08b2082ee6b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381030 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381030 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381030 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e18f17c5-7c1e-57f7-8c6c-914f7ad84ff8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381031 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y-3}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381031 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381031 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "92f50e5a-02c5-577c-aef6-8553b78e20a0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381032 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{2y-3}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381032 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381032 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02529dfd-091f-5dfe-8f9c-f37ba8ceaee6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381033 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{2y-3}^{-{y}^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x,y)\\,dx\\,dy" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381033 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186381033 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "eeb3ceb7-f1b3-5f08-8d14-04c619324de8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81381" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate ${∬}_{D}y{e}^{x}\\,dA,$ where $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e5ab0ab-75de-56ed-a439-c354130b3e57" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382490 #edb/ref 1074 "The integral is defined over a type II region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 2-{y}^{2}}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y{e}^{x}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}(y\\cdot {e}^{x})\\,dx\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}(y\\cdot {e}^{x})\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}{e}^{x}\\,dx]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{e}^{x}]_{{y}^{2}}^{2-{y}^{2}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y({e}^{2-{y}^{2}}-{e}^{{y}^{2}})dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(y{e}^{2-{y}^{2}}-y{e}^{{y}^{2}})\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(y{e}^{2-{y}^{2}}-y{e}^{{y}^{2}})\\,dy & ={[-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2-{y}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{1}+{e}^{1}-({e}^{2}+{e}^{0})) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-2e+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186382496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382491 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c47442ae-5527-5caf-9a94-06d41bf2c9e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382492 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382492 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382492 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "564a011e-7d84-5afe-b400-660c22c62607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382493 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1-{e}^{2}}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382493 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382493 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9eeb7da5-02bc-53cd-8e9b-696b1ca81db9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382494 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382494 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382494 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c88a38f3-dfb9-5885-a772-66802526c4bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382495 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{2}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382495 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382495 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d4831a22-e864-59f2-ae77-cad6d38daf40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382496 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{{e}^{2}-2e+1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382496 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382496 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "066b28e3-9cf3-5ff6-8a91-a6102f1fe87b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186382595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1069 "q-89550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d6/d6f00e63a577dff29021e50add69cf916b3f74ed90530b5f4c9f46295950b416.png)\n\nEvaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{x}^{3}\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D$ is the region enclosed between the curves $4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4,$ above the $x$-axis, as shown in the picture." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f13b8b49-8217-594e-a1e7-695fd01b0cfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382594 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $D$ is a type II region. Since $x\\ge 0,$ we obtain the following equations in terms of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4 & \\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's determine the limits of integration.\n\n- To determine the $y$-limits, we need to find the $y$-coordinates of the points at which the curves intersect. So, we set the following equation and solve it for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}} & =\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}} \\\\ 1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =4-{y}^{2} \\\\ 4-{y}^{2} & =16-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{y}^{2} & =12 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, since our region lies above the $x$-axis, the $y$-limits are \n$0\\le y\\le 2.$\n\n- To determine the left and right functions, we draw a horizontal arrow from left to right through the region, as usual.\n\n![](images/ec/ec8853d64b58c40935b769745d5adb9ebc5c84b7f9407cc93dff4b809ed64ad5.png)\n\nAs a result, we get\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\sqrt{1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}{x}^{3}\\,dA={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\,{x}^{3}\\,dx]\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,{[\\,\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}\\,]}_{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}/4}}^{\\sqrt{4-{y}^{2}}}\\text{ }dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\frac{1}{4}[{(4-{y}^{2})}^{2}-{(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4})}^{2}]dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,[(16-8{y}^{2}+{y}^{4})-(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})]dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(15-\\frac{15}{2}{y}^{2}+\\frac{15}{16}{y}^{4})dy \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15}{4}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,(1-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{4}}{16})dy & =\\frac{15}{4}{[y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{5}}{80}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}[(2-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2}{5})-0] \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382596 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186382600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186382598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186382595 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "95f530d4-be17-5a5f-8b00-55f168260743" #edb/ref 1759218